Task:
A maintainer on the project EffortlessMetrics/perl-lsp-swarm (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #9449: ci(workflows): retire orphaned temporary workflows and reconcile authority

Parent: #8055
Train: #8686 A09
Depends on: #9448
Routing/enforcement: #3048 / #4787 / #4789
Release consumers: #6055 / #8576

## One-PR objective

Perform the first evidence-backed retirement/authority cleanup using #9448's inventory. Disable or delete only workflows proven orphaned, expired, obsolete, or duplicative; preserve useful specialized workflows with current owners.

For every changed workflow, record inventory classification, current callers/consumers, replacement or retirement reason, retained historical evidence location, context/policy references, and rollback/recovery where disabling rather than deletion is chosen.

Reconcile:

- orphan/expired temporary workflows;
- obsolete reusable workflows with no active caller;
- duplicate context producers;
- stale checked-in required-check references;
- authoritative workflow callers/consumers;
- historical evidence so executable YAML is not retained only for archaeology.

Deletion count is not a goal.

## Negative controls

- delete workflow still called by authoritative path;
- remove stable context without policy/consumer update;
- retire specialized workflow solely because it is uncommon;
- leave expired temporary workflow executable;
- delete workflow whose only historical evidence has not been preserved;
- source retirement contradicts live enablement/consumer state but is represented complete.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Every orphaned/expired workflow found in the first #9448 inventory has a reviewed terminal disposition.
- [ ] Active callers/policy/context references are reconciled before removal.
- [ ] Historical evidence survives outside obsolete executable YAML where needed.
- [ ] Canonical PR/main/nightly/candidate/publication/verification authority is easier to identify and unchanged except by reviewed transition.
- [ ] Live state uncertainty remains `not_proven`; no GitHub settings are silently mutated.

## Codex end goal

Land the first retirement/reconciliation PR only. Do not chase an arbitrary workflow count or remove useful specialized lanes to make the inventory smaller.

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""Workflow authority reconciliation.

Models the first retirement/authority cleanup PR: an inventory of
workflows is classified, callers/consumers are traced via typed edges,
and a walker reconciles authority by walking the dependency graph,
detecting orphans, duplicates, and stale references — the same
recursion the original hand-rolled machinery struggled to express.
"""

# ---------- entities ----------

node Workflow {
    has name: str = "";
    has kind: str = "";        # "temp" | "reusable" | "context" | "specialized"
    has classification: str = ""; # orphan | expired | obsolete | duplicate | active | not_proven
    has evidence_kept: bool = False; # historical evidence preserved outside YAML
}

node Caller {
    has name: str = "";        # PR / main / nightly / candidate / publication / verification
    has enabled: bool = True;
}

edge Invokes { }            # Caller -> Workflow
edge Produces { }           # Workflow -> Workflow (context producer)
edge Replaces { }           # Workflow -> Workflow (replacement link)

# ---------- walker: reconcile authority by walking the dependency graph ----------

walker Reconciler {
    has visited: list[str] = [];   # cycle guard — explicit, per jac 0.36.1
    has report_lines: list[str] = [];

    can start with Root entry {
        print("=== Workflow authority reconciliation ===");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can sweep with Caller entry {
        label = "live" if here.enabled else "disabled";
        line = f"caller[{label}] {here.name}";
        self.report_lines.append(line);
        visit [->:Invokes:->];
    }

    can review with Workflow entry {
        # cycle policy: do not re-inspect a workflow we've already classified
        if here.name in self.visited {
            self.report_lines.append(f"  [cycle] skip {here.name}");
            disengage;
        }
        self.visited.append(here.name);

        status = "OK" if here.classification == "active" else "REVIEW";
        line = f"wf[{status}] {here.name} kind={here.kind} class={here.classification}";
        self.report_lines.append(line);

        if here.classification in ["orphan", "expired", "obsolete", "duplicate"] {
            action = "disable" if not here.evidence_kept else "delete-after-archive";
            self.report_lines.append(f"  -> retire: {action}");
        } else {
            self.report_lines.append("  -> keep");
        }

        # only safe to walk Produces (context dependencies) if not retiring;
        # still walk to surface stale references for the inventory
        visit [->:Replaces:->];
        visit [->:Produces:->];
    }

    # fall-through: if a workflow is reached but the walker has no
    # `with Workflow` ability on the current frontier type, keep moving.
    can fallback with Workflow entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can finish with Root entry {
        print("--- inventory walk ---");
        for ln in self.report_lines {
            print(ln);
        }
        print(f"--- reviewed {len(self.visited)} workflow(s) ---");
        print("live state uncertainty: not_proven (no GitHub settings mutated)");
    }
}

# ---------- demonstration graph ----------

with entry {
    # callers (authority lanes)
    pr_lane = Caller(name="pr", enabled=True);
    main_lane = Caller(name="main", enabled=True);
    nightly = Caller(name="nightly", enabled=True);
    candidate = Caller(name="candidate", enabled=True);
    publication = Caller(name="publication", enabled=True);
    verification = Caller(name="verification", enabled=True);

    # workflows with classifications from the #9448 inventory
    wf_pr_build = Workflow(name="pr-build", kind="temp", classification="active", evidence_kept=True);
    wf_main_release = Workflow(name="main-release", kind="reusable", classification="active", evidence_kept=True);
    wf_nightly_smoke = Workflow(name="nightly-smoke", kind="temp", classification="active", evidence_kept=True);
    wf_orphan_temp = Workflow(name="orphan-temp-2019", kind="temp", classification="orphan", evidence_kept=True);
    wf_expired = Workflow(name="expired-rotation-2022", kind="temp", classification="expired", evidence_kept=True);
    wf_obsolete = Workflow(name="obsolete-reusable-no-caller", kind="reusable", classification="obsolete", evidence_kept=True);
    wf_dup_ctx = Workflow(name="dup-context-producer", kind="context", classification="duplicate", evidence_kept=True);
    wf_specialized = Workflow(name="specialized-coverage", kind="specialized", classification="active", evidence_kept=True);

    # wire the graph: callers invoke workflows; context producers feed consumers
    pr_lane +>:Invokes:+> wf_pr_build;
    main_lane +>:Invokes:+> wf_main_release;
    nightly +>:Invokes:+> wf_nightly_smoke;
    candidate +>:Invokes:+> wf_pr_build;
    publication +>:Invokes:+> wf_main_release;
    verification +>:Invokes:+> wf_specialized;

    # replacement / production relationships surface obsolete + duplicate
    wf_obsolete +>:Replaces:+> wf_main_release;
    wf_dup_ctx +>:Produces:+> wf_pr_build;
    wf_dup_ctx +>:Produces:+> wf_nightly_smoke;

    # attach everything to root for traversal
    root ++> pr_lane
        ++> main_lane
        ++> nightly
        ++> candidate
        ++> publication
        ++> verification
        ++> wf_orphan_temp
        ++> wf_expired
        ++> wf_specialized;

    # spawn the reconciler
    root spawn Reconciler();
}
