However:

In many Redfish URLs, the last segment is a static resource or operation type (e.g. /redfish/v1/Systems/{ComputerSystemId}/EthernetInterfaces has EthernetInterfaces as the last segment).
If a workflow modifies EthernetInterfaces on System.Embedded.1 and System.Embedded.2, the target list will be ["EthernetInterfaces", "EthernetInterfaces"].
The unique targets count becomes 1 instead of 2. The dynamic blast radius calculations under-evaluate risk when targeting different physical assets if they perform similar operations.
Proposed Solution
