Issue #26: 26. Project dashboard

## Goal

A project member can see what needs attention now and follow open actions across retrospectives.

## Scope

- Extend project detail with the current COLLECTING cycle and the viewer's feedback link/status, active/upcoming retrospective links, completed retrospective history and confirmed OPEN actions across the project.
- Use live project-scoped queries for actions, not copied rows per cycle. Include owner, optional due date and link to the originating summary/topic.
- Provide the authorized action OPEN/DONE operation from #17, including its explicitly agreed post-COMPLETE behavior.
- Use Django templates and HTMX partials; enforce all project/stage visibility in querysets/selectors.

## Acceptance criteria

These criteria include the documented PM defaults below. Where a product decision is marked **Needs agreement**, settle it before implementing the affected behavior.

- [ ] Members see only their own projects, cycles, retrospective links and actions; cross-project IDs expose nothing.
- [ ] Before REVEAL, submission status reveals no other member's card text, category counts, anonymity choices or exact submission timestamps.
- [ ] After reveal, aggregate participation is read from CycleParticipation and is labelled as submission participation rather than attendance.
- [ ] The current cycle and active retro remain distinct when a new collection cycle coexists with an older DISCUSS retrospective.
- [ ] Confirmed OPEN actions remain visible across later cycles; DRAFT and DONE actions are excluded from the open list, and updating status immediately changes the list.
- [ ] No-cycle/no-history/no-actions and unassigned draft-free states have clear empty views; permitted action links lead to the correct project/retro.

## Decisions and unresolved choices

### Submission visibility

- **Status/source:** PM proposal; needs agreement.
- **Reason:** The dashboard calls for submission status, while pre-reveal privacy must not expose other members' cards.
- **Consequence:** Show own status before REVEAL and full aggregate participation afterwards. Any facilitator-only early roster status needs an explicit decision.

## Assumptions and implementation defaults

PM proposal: before REVEAL show only the viewer's own submitted/not-submitted status on the dashboard; show the full per-member aggregate snapshot after reveal. The historical dashboard asks for submission status but does not define pre-reveal visibility. This preserves the stricter pre-reveal data-minimization rule; record any desired facilitator-only roster status as a product decision before exposing it.

## Dependencies and implementation notes

#5, #7-#10, #17 and #25; identity sign-in remains a scheduling decision while #4 is post-MVP.

Build one project-authorized selector/query layer, then sections and HTMX action refresh. Order cycle/history deterministically; sort open actions by due date (undated last) then stable ID under the proposed default.

## Out of scope

Cross-project analytics, reminders, calendars, copied action backlogs, new project settings and attendance/performance scoring.

Excluded work stays documented here for review; no follow-up issue is created by this grooming pass.

## Constraints

Follow AGENTS.md: authorization predicates in `projects/permissions.py`; filter private data before rendering; stage writes only through `advance_stage()`; every board mutation bumps version transactionally and returns full viewer-filtered state. Django/HTMX outside the React board. PostgreSQL is the only application infrastructure. New settings come from environment variables plus `.env.example`. Add no dependency without approval; approved Python dependencies must be exactly pinned with `uv.lock` synced. Tests live in `tests/` with `config/settings_test.py`. Do not change product scope/design documents incidentally.

## Validation

Use `tests/test_dashboard.py` for project boundaries, pre-reveal response omissions, multiple cycles, live action carry-over and allowed status changes. Inspect HTML/HTMX output and run suite/ruff checks.

## Scheduling and readiness

MVP backlog scope, excluding user-deferred #4. Groomed for scope review; implementation is not started by this update. Dependencies, dependency-installation approvals, and any explicitly unresolved decisions above are implementation gates, not reasons to omit this issue from the groomed backlog.

