- the policy is identical across DualDAG-Advisory and DualDAG-Authority;
- the policy does not change by scenario/perturbation family unless a separate pre-registered policy ablation explicitly studies that change;
- thresholds/trust/corroboration rules are not tuned after observing final benchmark results;
- every witness/admissibility/permit artifact records the policy identity/version used;
- a policy revision affecting witness validity is treated as a relevant permit dependency under #509;
- any policy sensitivity study is reported separately from the primary result.

The primary protocol should include concrete frozen semantics for representative cases such as direct actor-visible observations, trusted tool results, unverified peer reports, corroborated reports, unresolved contradictions, and explicitly superseded evidence. The final exact rules come from #508; #511 must not silently redefine them.

