Task:
A maintainer on the project Growth-Circle/cadis (Rust) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #259: fix(core): prevent symlink cycles in SearchIndex::build

## Problem

`SearchIndex::build` in `crates/cadis-core/src/search_index.rs:44-72` walks the workspace iteratively using `entry.metadata()` (which follows symlinks) with no canonicalization and no visited set. A symlink pointing to an ancestor directory re-pushes the same real directory forever. Issue #232 covers `search_files` in `tools.rs` only — verified against the issue body — not this index-build path.

## Actual Output

Any workspace containing a self-referential symlink (e.g. `ln -s . loop`) makes the first `file.search` (index built lazily at `lib.rs:4976-4979`) loop forever, consuming CPU/memory until the daemon is killed — a safe-read tool that needs no approval.

## How to Fix

Track canonicalized visited directories in a `HashSet` and/or add a depth cap during the index walk (mirroring the #232 fix), and add a unit test with a symlink-cycle fixture (Windows: junction).

## Expected Output

Index builds terminate on workspaces with symlink cycles; `file.search` returns results instead of hanging.

## Critical Level

Medium

## My Confidence

High

## Why Matters?

Availability: the same exploit family as #232 but through a different, unguarded code path that stays open after the #232 fix.


Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""Symlink-cycle-safe workspace indexer.

Models the core scenario from cadis issue #259: walking a workspace
graph where symlinks can re-create parent directories. A naive walker
loops forever; the idiomatic walker carries an explicit cycle policy
(canonicalized visited set + depth cap) so the build terminates.
"""

node Dir {
    has name: str = "";
    has canonical_id: str = "";
}

node File {
    has name: str = "";
    has size: int = 0;
}

edge Parent {
    has link_name: str = "";
}

edge LoopLink {
    has target: str = "";
}

walker IndexBuilder {
    has root_label: str = "";
    has max_depth: int = 16;
    has seen: list[str] = [];
    has indexed_files: int = 0;

    can start with Root entry {
        print(f"IndexBuilder starting for {self.root_label} (max_depth={self.max_depth})");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can descend with Dir entry {
        if self.max_depth <= 0 {
            print(f"[DEPTH-CAP] dropping into {here.name} would exceed limit; disengaging");
            disengage;
        }
        if here.canonical_id in self.seen {
            print(f"[CYCLE] refusing to re-enter canonical {here.canonical_id} via symlink");
            disengage;
        }
        self.seen.append(here.canonical_id);
        print(f"[ENTER] dir {here.name} (canon={here.canonical_id}) depth={self.max_depth}");
        self.max_depth -= 1;
        visit [->:Parent:->] else { disengage; }
    }

    can record with File entry {
        self.indexed_files += 1;
        print(f"[FILE] {here.name} ({here.size} bytes)");
        visit [->:Parent:->] else { disengage; }
    }
}

with entry {
    workspace = Dir(name="workspace", canonical_id="real:/workspace");
    src = Dir(name="src", canonical_id="real:/workspace/src");
    docs = Dir(name="docs", canonical_id="real:/workspace/docs");
    loop = Dir(name="loop", canonical_id="real:/workspace/loop");

    main_rs = File(name="main.rs", size=2048);
    readme = File(name="README.md", size=512);
    notes = File(name="notes.txt", size=128);

    root ++> workspace;
    workspace +>:Parent(link_name="src"):+> src;
    workspace +>:Parent(link_name="docs"):+> docs;
    workspace +>:Parent(link_name="loop"):+> loop;

    src +>:Parent:+> main_rs;
    docs +>:Parent:+> readme;
    loop +>:Parent:+> notes;

    loop +>:LoopLink(target="/workspace"):+> workspace;

    builder = IndexBuilder(root_label="cadis-workspace", max_depth=8);
    workspace spawn builder;

    print(f"\nIndexBuilder terminated. Files indexed: {builder.indexed_files}");
    print(f"Visited canonical dirs: {builder.seen}");
}
