models that four-layer pipeline as four node archetypes connected by
typed `Next` edges, then walks it with two walkers:

- FullReaper does the O(n)-per-layer recompute the issue complains about.
- TailWeaver takes the incremental fast path: only the last message is
  rebuilt; the prefix is reused by reference.

The comparison prints how many nodes each walker had to visit to deliver
the same visible tail.
"""

# ---------- entity archetypes ----------

node Block {
    has block_id: str = "";
    has kind: str = "text";     # text | tool_use | tool_result
    has text: str = "";
    has is_delta: bool = False; # the streaming tail block being edited
