Task:
A maintainer on the project Yuxin-Ren-SZ/Yuxin_MEA (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #6: [Workflow] Persist and version pipeline task graph definitions

## Description
Pipeline task dependencies are registered at runtime in `_forward_deps`, while cached task records also store dependency lists that are not used for scheduling. After a restart, dependency behavior depends on what the caller registers again. Missing or changed registration can make cached tasks appear dependency-free or otherwise inconsistent.

Relevant code:
- `pipeline_manager/manager.py`: `_forward_deps` and `_reverse_deps`
- `pipeline_manager/task_record.py`: persisted dependency field
- `pipeline_manager/manager.py`: `_deps_complete()` reads the runtime dependency registry

## Suggested approach
Persist a versioned task graph or pipeline definition. On load, validate cached task records against the registered definition. If dependencies or task versions changed, mark affected tasks stale or require an explicit migration/reset.

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""Versioned task pipeline: persist task definitions as a graph and validate cached records after a restart.

Models the essential scenario from Yuxin-Ren-SZ/Yuxin_MEA issue #6:
- Tasks are registered at runtime in a forward-dependency registry.
- Cached task records carry dependency lists that are NOT the scheduling source.
- After a "restart" (re-loading a new graph), stale cached records must be detected
  and invalidated when the registered definition diverges from the persisted one.
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Archetypes
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# A persisted task definition. The `version` field is what makes the graph
# "versioned" — when a task's definition changes, its version bumps, and any
# cached record pinned to an older version is now stale.
node TaskDef {
    has name: str = "";
    has version: int = 1;
}

# A cached, run-time task record. It remembers a snapshot of the dependency
# list it was last computed against plus the version of the TaskDef it was
# pinned to. In the issue, this record is what gets persisted across restarts
# while the real graph is re-registered by callers.
node TaskRecord {
    has name: str = "";
    has pinned_version: int = 0;
    has cached_deps: list[str] = [];
}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Typed edges — the relationship carries meaning, so it gets a name.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# "TaskDef `a` depends on TaskDef `b`" — the registration-time forward edge.
edge Dep {}

# "Cached record `r` was computed against TaskDef `a` at this version" —
# a pointer from a cached record to the definition it pinned to.
edge PinnedTo {}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Walker: graph audit
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

walker Auditor {
    has stale: list[str] = [];

    can start with Root entry {
        # Step 1: walk every TaskDef → TaskRecord link and check each record's
        # pinned version against the live definition version.
        visit [->:PinnedTo:->];
    }

    can audit with TaskDef entry {
        # One record is reachable per PinnedTo edge out of this TaskDef.
        for record in [->:PinnedTo:->] {
            record_name = record.name;
            record_version = record.pinned_version;
            live_version = here.version;
            deps_match = record.cached_deps == [->:Dep:->].name;
            if record_version != live_version or not deps_match {
                self.stale.append(record_name);
            }
        }
        visit [->:Dep:->];
    }

    can report with Root entry {
        if self.stale {
            print(f"STALE records requiring re-migration: {self.stale}");
        } else {
            print("All cached records match the registered definition.");
        }
    }
}

walker DependencyOrder {
    has order: list[str] = [];
    has visiting: list[str] = [];

    can start with Root entry {
        visit [->:Dep:->];
    }

    can order with TaskDef entry {
        # Cycle guard — explicit because Jac 0.36.1 walkers do NOT dedupe.
        if here.name in self.visiting {
            print(f"CYCLE detected at {here.name}; aborting walk.");
            disengage;
        }
        self.visiting.append(here.name);
        # Recurse into dependencies first, then append.
        if [->:Dep:->] {
            visit [->:Dep:->];
        }
        self.order.append(here.name);
        self.visiting.pop();
    }
}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo wiring
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

with entry {
