I'm writing an order auditor in Jac and need both flavors of early return working side by side. Orders are nodes with an amount, a validity flag, and a fraud flag. Invalid orders should be skipped while the audit continues to later orders, but a flagged-fraud order must halt the whole walk on the spot. Print a line per order showing which action fired.

```jac
"""Order auditor: invalid orders are skipped, fraudulent orders halt the audit.

Orders are nodes carrying an amount, a validity flag, and a fraud flag.
The auditor walker traverses a chain of orders and reacts differently:

  - A *valid* order is recorded and traversal continues.
  - An *invalid* order is skipped (early return from the ability) but the
    walker still moves on to the next order.
  - A *fraudulent* order halts the entire audit on the spot via
    ``disengage;`` — no further orders are visited.

This places the two flavors of early-return side by side: ability-level
``return;`` to skip one node, and walker-level ``disengage;`` to abort the
walk.
"""

node Order {
    has title: str = "";
    has amount: float = 0.0;
    has valid: bool = True;
    has fraud: bool = False;
}

walker Auditor {
    has label: str = "Q4";
    has reviewed: int = 0;
    has halted_on_fraud: bool = False;

    can start with Root entry {
        print(f"Auditor '{self.label}' starting review of pending orders");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can review with Order entry {
        # Fraud halts the entire walk — no further orders get visited.
        if here.fraud {
            print(f"[HALT] fraud flag on '{here.title}' (${here.amount:.2f}) — disengaging");
            self.halted_on_fraud = True;
            disengage;
        }

        # Invalid orders are skipped, but traversal continues.
        if not here.valid {
            print(f"[SKIP] invalid order '{here.title}' — continuing audit");
            visit [-->];
            return;
        }

        # Valid order: record it and move on.
        self.reviewed += 1;
        print(f"[REVIEW] '{here.title}' amount=${here.amount:.2f}");
        visit [-->];
    }
}

with entry {
