A maintainer on the project dimensionalOS/dimos (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #3493: Follow person agentic blueprint issue

Discord user was not able to run our unitree-go2-agentic blueprint, [link to the message thread](<https://discord.com/channels/1341146487186391173/1536832724491313282/1536832724491313282>)


**Found & fixed these three issues last week:**

* **Transport env-var naming bug**: `default.env` set `TRANSPORTS__BROKER__*` unconditionally, breaking any blueprint that doesn't declare a `broker` transport (`Unknown transport configuration section(s): broker`). Fixed in `merge_environment` to skip transport env vars for transports the blueprint doesn't use. PR #3445, merged.
* **Qwen VL model dead**: default model `qwen2.5-vl-72b-instruct` returns 403 access_denied, deprecated/restricted on Alibaba's side. Switched default to `qwen-vl-max`. PR #3448, merged.
* **edgetam-dimos PyPI package broken**: the published sdist is missing `sam2/csrc/connected_components.cu`, so the CUDA extension can never build for anyone; tracker silently falls back to slow unaccelerated mode and loses the person after a short time. PR #3456, merged.

---
