A maintainer on the project illegalstudio/elephc (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #635: provisional_variant_group_sig still seeds return type as PhpType::Int

## Summary

`Checker::provisional_variant_group_sig` still hardcodes the provisional return type to `PhpType::Int` for conditionally-declared function variant groups. Free-function recursion already seeds the provisional signature from the declared return hint via `provisional_return_type()` (see PR #626), but this sibling path was intentionally left alone.

## Location

- `src/types/checker/driver/functions.rs` — `provisional_variant_group_sig`
- Provisional insert site: same file, when resolving a variant group before individual variants are fully resolved
- Contrast with the fixed free-function path: `src/types/checker/functions/resolution/signature.rs` — `provisional_return_type`

## Why it matters

The provisional signature is published so a self-call (or a mutual-recursion re-entry) can be typed while the body is still being walked. When that placeholder is always `Int`:

- a recursive / mutually recursive free function that is only reachable through a **variant group** (conditionally-declared functions) and returns non-`int` can fail to compile or mis-type the self-call expression
- the bad type can leak into argument checking at the self-call site and to outside callers, the same shape PR #626 fixed for ordinary free functions

Methods were never affected by the free-function bug (class schema already seeds the declared type). Variant groups are the remaining provisional-`Int` hole called out in #626.

## Suggested fix

Reuse the same resolution order as `provisional_return_type`:

1. body contains `yield` → `Generator`
2. else explicit return hint → resolve the declared hint
3. else keep the historical unhinted `Int` placeholder
4. unresolvable hint → fall back to `Int` and let the authoritative pass report the real diagnostic

Avoid inventing a second provisional policy.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Conditional / variant-group recursive functions with non-`int` return hints compile and type like ordinary free-function recursion
- [ ] Mutual recursion through a variant group preserves the declared return type for self-calls
- [ ] Negative controls still reject a recursive body whose base case disagrees with the hint
- [ ] Regression tests covering at least: hinted `: string` / `: array` / object return, unhinted base-case inference, generator, and a wrong-base-case diagnostic
- [ ] No change to method / class-schema provisional behaviour

## Origin

Follow-up from the PR #626 review. Deliberately not fixed in that branch; listed in the PR caveats as the most likely sibling of the free-function recursion bug.

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""Provisional return-type seeding for variant-group recursion.

Models the issue's core scenario: conditionally-declared function variant
groups whose provisional signature is hardcoded to Int, breaking recursive
self-calls through a variant group when the declared return hint is not Int.
The demo shows the fixed resolution order (yield -> hint -> Int fallback)
applied at the variant-group join site, while free-function recursion
continues to work unchanged and method/class recursion is unaffected.

Entities:
  - FuncDecl: a function declaration node carrying its declared return hint.
  - VariantGroup: a conditionally-declared bundle of function variants.
  - CallSite: a self-call or mutual-recursion re-entry inside a body.
  - ReturnKind: the three resolution sources (yield, hint, fallback).

The walker `ProvisionalTyper` walks every FuncDecl reachable from root,
classifies each declaration by which return-kind wins, and publishes the
provisional return type for the variant-group join so self-calls type-check.
"""

node ReturnKind {
    has label: str = "";
    has chosen: str = "";
}

node FuncDecl {
    has name: str = "";
    has has_yield: bool = False;
    has return_hint: str = "";
    has hint_resolvable: bool = True;
    has provisional: str = "";
    has source: str = "";
}

node VariantGroup {
    has group_name: str = "";
    has joined_provisional: str = "";
    has joined_source: str = "";
}

node CallSite {
    has caller: str = "";
    has observed_type: str = "";
}

edge Declares { }
edge JoinsVariant { }
edge Invokes { }
edge YieldsFrom { }
edge ReturnsHint { }

walker ProvisionalTyper {
    has unresolved_hints: list[str] = [];

    can start with Root entry {
        print("Resolving provisional return types for declared functions");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can resolve with FuncDecl entry {
        picked = here.pick_provisional();
        here.provisional = picked[0];
        here.source = picked[1];
        print(f"{here.name}: provisional={here.provisional} via {here.source}");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can join_group with VariantGroup entry {
        kinds: list[list[str]] = [];
        for child in [->:Declares:->] {
            kinds.append([child.provisional, child.source]);
        }
        joined = here.merge_kinds(kinds);
        here.joined_provisional = joined[0];
        here.joined_source = joined[1];
        print(f"variant group {here.group_name}: joined={here.joined_provisional} via {here.joined_source}");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can verify with CallSite entry {
        here.observed_type = here.expected_observation();
        marker = "OK" if here.observed_type == here.expected_observation() else "FAIL";
        print(f"[{marker}] call from {here.caller}: observed={here.observed_type}");
    }
}

with entry {
    # Three resolution sources for the provisional seed.
    generator_kind = ReturnKind(label="yield");
    hinted_kind = ReturnKind(label="hint");
    fallback_kind = ReturnKind(label="fallback");

    # Free-function recursion path: already seeds from declared hint (PR #626).
    free_hinted = FuncDecl(
        name="free_hinted",
        has_yield=False,
        return_hint="string",
        hint_resolvable=True,
    );

    # Variant group: a conditionally-declared bundle of variants.
    grp = VariantGroup(group_name="cond_group");

    # Variant that yields -> Generator wins.
    gen_variant = FuncDecl(
        name="gen_variant",
        has_yield=True,
        return_hint="",
        hint_resolvable=True,
    );

    # Variant with a declared `: array` hint.
    arr_variant = FuncDecl(
        name="arr_variant",
        has_yield=False,
        return_hint="array",
        hint_resolvable=True,
    );

    # Variant with no hint: historical Int placeholder.
    unhinted_variant = FuncDecl(
        name="unhinted_variant",
        has_yield=False,
        return_hint="",
        hint_resolvable=True,
    );

    # Variant whose hint is unresolvable: stays Int, diagnostic surfaces later.
    bad_hint_variant = FuncDecl(
        name="bad_hint_variant",
        has_yield=False,
        return_hint="WeirdType",
        hint_resolvable=False,
    );

    # Method/class-schema recursion already works (control: unaffected).
    method_decl = FuncDecl(
        name="method_on_class",
        has_yield=False,
        return_hint="object",
        hint_resolvable=True,
    );

    # Self-call sites to verify the provisional type holds for the join.
    gen_call = CallSite(caller="gen_variant");
    arr_call = CallSite(caller="arr_variant");
    free_call = CallSite(caller="free_hinted");
    method_call = CallSite(caller="method_on_class");
    bad_call = CallSite(caller="bad_hint_variant");

    # Wire the graph: root -> variant group + standalone decls.
    root ++> grp;
    grp +>:Declares:+> gen_variant;
    grp +>:Declares:+> arr_variant;
    grp +>:Declares:+> unhinted_variant;
    grp +>:Declares:+> bad_hint_variant;
    root ++> free_hinted;
    root ++> method_decl;

    # Self-call edges from each variant to its CallSite.
    gen_variant +>:Invokes:+> gen_call;
    arr_variant +>:Invokes:+> arr_call;
    free_hinted +>:Invokes:+> free_call;
    method_decl +>:Invokes:+> method_call;
    bad_hint_variant +>:Invokes:+> bad_call;

    # Walk the graph, resolving provisionals then verifying call sites.
    root spawn ProvisionalTyper();

    print("\nSummary of variant-group join resolution order:");
    print(f"  yield wins   -> {gen_variant.provisional} ({gen_variant.source})");
    print(f"  hint wins    -> {arr_variant.provisional} ({arr_variant.source})");
    print(f"  no hint      -> {unhinted_variant.provisional} ({unhinted_variant.source})");
    print(f"  bad hint     -> {bad_hint_variant.provisional} ({bad_hint_variant.source})");
    print(f"  free func    -> {free_hinted.provisional} ({free_hinted.source})");
    print(f"  method/class -> {method_decl.provisional} ({method_decl.source})");
}
