A maintainer on the project memrynote/memry (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #1803: [mobile] T127: Performance re-verification on the release build: G2 <5 s and G3 <50 ms numbers re-measured on the reference device (Constitution V: regression blocks release)

> **Memry Mobile — Vault Parity Mobile App** · task `T127` · Phase 14 of 14 · gate **G6**

## Task

**`T127`** — Performance re-verification on the release build: G2 <5 s and G3 <50 ms numbers re-measured on the reference device (Constitution V: regression blocks release)

## Phase context — Phase 14: Polish & Store Prep — Train Phases 6–7 (Gate **G6** → submission)

**Purpose**: Cross-cutting quality + review-ready build.

**Checkpoint — G6**: archive validates with zero errors; external TestFlight approved; accessibility pass. Then submit.

## Ordering & dependencies

- **Train gates are serial** (Constitution): a phase does not start until the prior gate is green *with evidence*. Parallelism exists **within** a phase only.
- Polish & Store Prep runs after **G5**. Performance re-verification (T127) re-measures the G2 and G3 numbers — a regression blocks release (Constitution V).
