Framing worth carrying, because it sets the care level: this residue is the byproduct of a mechanism *working*. The distinct-reviewer asks fired correctly and repeatedly — they blocked TORQUE:1200, blocked TORQUE:1208 when a second review was queued onto the same Worker, and disqualified a Worker that became a code author. The leftover cards are the trace of checks firing, being satisfied, and having no way to record their own satisfaction. This is the maintenance path for a load-bearing safety mechanism, not cleanup after a defect.

## Required outcome

Bounded, authorized reconciliation of stale covered/superseded descendants and roots across product-proposal, Engineer-created, and system-derived task chains, without widening generic task mutation authority.

**Dry run (`apply=false`) is mutation-free and is the mandatory first step.** It accepts only an explicit bounded task-id list and returns deterministic per-task results. One ineligible item must not suppress results for others. Each task reports independently as eligible or ineligible with structured reasons, proposed covering evidence/task, current and final lane, and authority basis.

**Apply (`apply=true`)** may mutate only items the same caller is authorized to reconcile and whose durable lineage and evidence still match the dry-run boundary. Recheck authorization, task versions, coverage lineage, and terminal evidence atomically at apply time. Stale or racing inputs fail closed.

**Authority.** Preserve existing creator/owner/supervising-Architect boundaries. Grant no generic cross-Architect task writes. Define and test the narrow authority rule for system-derived descendants using their durable parent/owner chain rather than caller assertions or labels.

