Issue #30: [BUG] [NeoForge 1.21.1] StackOverflowError on chunk load: lazy BlockEntity creation in getBlockEntity() recurses with Data Anchor (Enhanced Celestials 2 dependency)

**Environment:** Minecraft 1.21.1, NeoForge 21.1.248, Swinging Lanterns 1.21.1-1.5.0.1, Data Anchor 2.0.0.16 (library shipped with Enhanced Celestials 2).

**Symptom:** the game crashes with `java.lang.StackOverflowError: Exception chunk generation/loading` the moment any chunk containing a hanging lantern loads. With a lantern near spawn the world becomes unenterable — the crash reproduces on every load attempt.

**Repro:**
1. Install Swinging Lanterns 1.5.0.1 and Data Anchor 2.0.0.16 (or Enhanced Celestials 2, which bundles it as a required dependency).
2. Place any supported hanging lantern, leave the area so the chunk unloads (or just save & quit).
3. Re-enter the world / walk back → StackOverflowError, repeating 6-frame cycle:

```
at LevelChunk.handler$swinginglanterns$ensureLanternBlockEntity(LevelChunk.java)
at LevelChunk.getBlockEntity(LevelChunk.java:354)
at LevelChunk.getBlockEntity(LevelChunk.java:325)
at LevelChunk.handler$dataanchor$dataAnchor$onSetBlockEntityHead(LevelChunk.java)
at LevelChunk.setBlockEntity(LevelChunk.java)
at LevelChunk.addAndRegisterBlockEntity(LevelChunk.java:358)
... (repeats until the stack overflows)
```

**Mechanism** (verified by disassembling both mods' mixins):

1. Your `WorldChunkMixin` injects at RETURN of `LevelChunk.getBlockEntity`: when the position holds a supported lantern and the result is null, it creates a `SwingingLanternBlockEntity` and calls `addAndRegisterBlockEntity` → `setBlockEntity`.
2. Data Anchor's `LevelChunkMixin` injects at HEAD of `setBlockEntity` and calls `getBlockEntity(pos)` there (it evicts the previous block entity from its ticking list).
3. That HEAD call happens **before** the new block entity reaches the `blockEntities` map, so `getBlockEntity` still returns null for the lantern position → your handler creates *another* block entity → `setBlockEntity` again → infinite mutual recursion.

**Suggested fix on your side:** make the lazy creation re-entrancy-safe — e.g. a ThreadLocal guard around the create+register block in `ensureLanternBlockEntity`, or checking a per-position "creation in progress" marker before creating. Creating and registering a block entity as a side effect of a getter is currently unprotected against any other mod that (legitimately) calls `getBlockEntity` from inside `setBlockEntity`/`removeBlockEntity` hooks — Data Anchor does it at HEAD of both.

I'm filing the mirror issue against Data Anchor as well (calling the public getter from a HEAD injection instead of reading the map directly); either side fixing their half breaks the loop, but both patterns are individually fragile.

**Our workaround** (modpack-local): a tiny mixin that cancels a *re-entrant* `addAndRegisterBlockEntity` for the same chunk+position on the same thread — happy to share it if useful.

Thanks for the mod — the lanterns are lovely!

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""Models the Swinging Lanterns / Data Anchor re-entrancy bug as a small
object-spatial program. Two mixins (``getBlockEntity`` and ``setBlockEntity``)
on a shared ``LevelChunk`` form a cycle that, without an explicit guard, would
recurse forever. The walker below walks the call graph exactly as the JVM
would, applies a per-position ThreadLocal-style guard, and reports whether the
state is safe.
"""

# --- Entities ---------------------------------------------------------------

node Hook {
    has name: str = "";
}

# The two mixins on LevelChunk. Each exposes the getter / setter the other
# will re-enter. They share a ``pos_key`` so the guard can key on position.
node GetBlockEntityMixin {
    has pos_key: str = "";
    has needs_lazy_create: bool = False;
}

node SetBlockEntityMixin {
    has pos_key: str = "";
    has evict_first: bool = False;
}

# The chunk that owns the block-entity map. Acts as a typed container: only
# nodes reachable via an ``OwnsMixin`` edge are its members.
node LevelChunk {
    has chunk_label: str = "";
}

# --- Edges ------------------------------------------------------------------
# All three relationships carry meaning, so each gets a typed archetype.

edge Calls { }
edge OwnsMixin { }
edge EvictsTo { }

# --- Walker -----------------------------------------------------------------

walker CallTracer {
    has guard_active: bool = False;
    has guarded_positions: list[str] = [];
    has recursion_depth: int = 0;
    has max_depth: int = 0;
    has crashed: bool = False;
    has safe: bool = False;
    has report: dict = {};

    can start with Root entry {
        print(f"Begin trace from chunk '{here.chunk_label}'");
        self.max_depth = 0;
        visit [-->];
    }

    # When we step onto the chunk, fan out to whichever mixin(s) it owns.
    can enter_chunk with LevelChunk entry {
        visit [->:OwnsMixin:->];
    }

    # Union ability: fires for either mixin type because both fields we read
    (``pos_key`` and the guard flag) live on a common base.
    can trace_calls
        with GetBlockEntityMixin | SetBlockEntityMixin entry {
        self.recursion_depth += 1;
        depth_now = self.recursion_depth;
        if depth_now > self.max_depth {
            self.max_depth = depth_now;
        }

        # Per-position guard: drop the call if we're already inside
        # ``ensureLanternBlockEntity`` for this position.
        already_guarded = False;
        for g in self.guarded_positions {
            if g == here.pos_key {
                already_guarded = True;
            }
        }
        if already_guarded {
            print(
                f"  depth={depth_now} GUARD drop re-entry on "
                f"{type(here).__name__}({here.pos_key})"
            );
            self.recursion_depth -= 1;
            return;
        }

        # Register this position as in-progress, then walk the outgoing
        # ``Calls`` edges that this mixin would make on the JVM thread.
        self.guarded_positions.append(here.pos_key);
        print(
            f"  depth={depth_now} enter "
            f"{type(here).__name__}({here.pos_key})"
        );
        visit [->:Calls:->];
        self.guarded_positions.pop();
        self.recursion_depth -= 1;
    }

    can finish with Root entry {
        depth_cap = 32;
        if self.max_depth > depth_cap {
            self.crashed = True;
            self.safe = False;
            verdict = "UNSAFE — would StackOverflowError";
        } else {
            self.crashed = False;
            self.safe = True;
            verdict = "safe — recursion bounded by per-position guard";
        }
        self.report = {
            "max_depth": self.max_depth,
            "crashed": self.crashed,
            "safe": self.safe,
            "guard_positions": list(self.guarded_positions),
        };
        print(
            f"Done: max_depth={self.max_depth} cap={depth_cap} → {verdict}"
        );
        print(f"Report: {self.report}");
    }
}

# --- Demo graph -------------------------------------------------------------
# Wire a chunk that owns one ``getBlockEntity`` mixin and one ``setBlockEntity``
# mixin. Their ``Calls`` edges form the mutual recursion from the bug report.

with entry {
    chunk = LevelChunk(chunk_label="spawn_chunk");
    get_mixin = GetBlockEntityMixin(
        pos_key="lantern@0,64,0", needs_lazy_create=True
    );
    set_mixin = SetBlockEntityMixin(
        pos_key="lantern@0,64,0", evict_first=True
    );

    # The chunk owns both mixins.
    chunk +>:OwnsMixin:+> get_mixin;
    chunk +>:OwnsMixin:+> set_mixin;

    # getBlockEntity → ensureLanternBlockEntity → setBlockEntity
    get_mixin +>:Calls:+> set_mixin;

    # setBlockEntity HEAD injection calls getBlockEntity → forms the cycle.
    set_mixin +>:Calls:+> get_mixin;

    # A plain hook is reachable from the chunk but is not part of the cycle,
    # so it confirms non-cycle edges do not crash the walker.
    hook = Hook(name="ambient_tick");
    chunk +>:OwnsMixin:+> hook;

    print("Spawning CallTracer on root →");
    tracer = CallTracer();
    root spawn tracer;
}
```

