Issue #124: Bound report workloads and define report cache coherence

## Problem

Several report endpoints materialize broad date ranges into Node and aggregate in memory, caches are process-local, and sales mutations invalidate dashboard keys but not the cited financial report keys.

## Audit Findings

* AUDIT-FINDING-017

## Evidence

- Broad range loads with in-memory expansion for financial, category-daily, user-performance, and daily reports:
  - `backend/src/reports/reports.service.ts:565-621,915-981,1118-1179,1269-1311`
- Dashboard executes twelve database operations on cache miss:
  - `backend/src/reports/reports.service.ts:679-763`
- Cache is process-local:
  - `backend/src/common/services/cache.service.ts:9-67`
- Sales mutation clears only dashboard cache keys:
  - `backend/src/sales/sales.service.ts:278,578`

## Impact

- Report latency and memory grow with tenant history.
- Financial results can remain cached after mutations until TTL.
- Multiple instances can produce inconsistent report values.

## Scope

- Reports module query boundaries and aggregation strategy.
- Report/dashboard cache keys and invalidation.
- Product search substring queries (as related evidence only).

## Out of Scope

- Hosted platform observability (AUDIT-FINDING-019).
- General operational policy (AUDIT-FINDING-019).

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Representative production-scale workload evidence (cardinalities, query plans, or timings) is collected before optimization decisions.
- [ ] Report endpoints have explicit, documented cost/range limits where appropriate.
- [ ] Cache invalidation is defined per report dependency and organization scope.
- [ ] Report behavior is deterministic across multiple instances or caches are explicitly per-instance with bounded staleness.
- [ ] Automated performance regression checks cover at least one broad-range report path.

## Dependencies

- AUDIT-FINDING-019 relates to operational observability evidence; coordinate measurements.

## SDD

This issue is an investigation and may become an SDD change depending on its outcome.

