Issue #132: Full typed GEDCOM model via schema-driven code generation

## Goal
Reach 100% typed coverage of the GEDCOM 5.5.1 + 7.0 registry (~479 structures) so a consumer can navigate the whole parsed document as a typed object graph (`$document->individuals[i]->bapm[0]->plac`, `…->sour[0]->source($document)->…`), with **no silent data loss** for unmodeled or extension tags.

The structural model classes are **generated from the vendored registry** (not hand-authored); only the grammar value objects (`DateValue`/`PlaceValue`/`AgeValue`) and the lazy pointer resolver stay hand-written.

## Measured scope
- 479 registry structures (195 × 5.5.1, 284 × 7.0); 318 container structures → classes, 161 leaves → typed properties; 52 pointer payloads, 14 enum payloads.
- Real-tree baseline: on a ~2150-individual tree, ~85% of tag occurrences are already typed; ~7.6% are standard tags not yet typed (closed by codegen) and ~7% are extensions (`_`-prefixed, preserved by the safety net).

## Key decisions
- **Directory layout:** kind-at-top, domain-within (`Model/Record/`, `Model/Substructure/{Event,Attribute,Name,Source,Place,Common}/`, `ValueObject/`, `Enumeration/`).
- **One merged, version-agnostic model** (7.0-only fields nullable under 5.5.1); no per-version split.
- **Shared substructure shapes reused** (one `EventDetail` family for all events), named property per tag.
- **Lazy pointer resolution:** pointer VO holds the xref; `->source($document): ?SourceRecord` resolves via a `GedcomDocument` xref index; `final readonly` preserved, no cycles stored.
- **Safety net:** every model class carries `list<RawSubstructure> $unknown` (a Model-layer leaf VO, no `Parse` dependency) for substructures the typed model does not consume — extensions and not-yet-typed tags are preserved and walkable.
- **Generator:** dev-only `tools/model-generator/` + `make generate-model`, `export-ignore` from the dist; committed output is the source of truth; a CI freshness gate (`git add -A && git diff --cached --quiet`) keeps the model in sync with the registry.

## Increments (each: plan → review → TDD → full audit → CI → merge)
- [x] **0 — Safety net:** ✅ merged (#133). `RawSubstructure` VO + mapper preserves unconsumed substructures + `$unknown` on the existing model classes. Stops silent loss now.
- [ ] **1 — Generator spike:** build the generator, validate on 3 structures (SourceCitation + BAPM via EventDetail + a PEDI-bearing child link), wire in.
- [ ] **2 — Full rollout:** generate all container classes + leaf properties across domains; migrate hand-written records to generated (preserving the public API); CI freshness gate.
- [ ] **3 — Polish:** lazy-resolver ergonomics, enum completeness, cross-version merge edges, README.

## Follow-ups
- Strict (throw-on-unknown) mode toggle threaded through the public API (deferred from increment 0).
- Preserve extensions nested under a **leaf** substructure (a scalar field such as `SEX`, or a parsed value object `DATE`/`PLAC`/`AGE`) — a leaf carries no `$unknown` today (documented boundary from increment 0).

