Diamonds in the dependency graph mean a task can be reached by multiple
paths, so we must audit each task exactly once. Walkers in jac 0.36.1 have
no built-in cycle/visited semantics (probe-verified), so we keep an
explicit guard set on the walker and traverse typed edges.
"""

node Task {
    has title: str = "";
    has minutes: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
}

edge DependsOn {}

walker BuildAuditor {
    has total_minutes: int = 0;
    has audited: set = {};

