Issue #721: scene validate: recurse into instanced sub-scenes for a composed verdict

## Parent

Follow-up from #664 (delivered by PR #720); the underlying dogfooding note is GDA-DF-040.

## What to build

`scene validate` checks only the scene file it is given: a `parent.tscn` that instances a broken child scene returns `valid: true` while the child's script and texture are missing (reproduced with a real engine during #720's review). GDA-DF-040's own case is a composed encounter scene, so an admission flow that gates on `scene validate` alone still infers a weaker static result than the scene's real load behavior. `scene preflight` does catch the broken child dynamically (`started: false`), so the pair covers the gap today — this issue closes it statically.

Extend `scene validate` so a scene's instanced sub-scenes are validated as part of the parent's verdict: resolve each `[ext_resource]` of type `PackedScene`, validate it with the same checks, and attribute each problem to the sub-scene file it was found in (so a problem inside `child.tscn` is not misread as a problem in `parent.tscn`). Decide and document the cycle/depth behavior (a scene cycle must terminate with a clear diagnostic, not hang) and whether an already-visited sub-scene is re-reported per instancing site or once per file.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `scene validate parent.tscn` reports the missing dependencies of an instanced child scene, attributed to the child file.
- [ ] A sub-scene cycle terminates with a structured diagnostic instead of recursing forever.
- [ ] A known-good composed scene still validates `valid: true`.
- [ ] e2e coverage on a composed known-bad and known-good scene pair.

## Blocked by

None - can start immediately.

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""Scene validate: recurse into instanced sub-scenes for a composed verdict.

Models the GDA-DF-040 dogfooding case: a parent scene instances child
scenes via PackedScene ext_resource references. A validator walker walks
the instancing graph, collecting per-scene problems so a missing
dependency in a child is attributed to the child file (not the parent).
A cycle guard mirrors the source's depth/visited policy so a cyclic
scene graph terminates with a structured diagnostic instead of looping
forever.
"""

node Scene {
    has path: str = "";
    has valid: bool = True;
    has problems: list[str] = [];

    can describe with Scene entry {
        label = "OK" if here.valid else "BAD";
        print(f"  [{label}] {here.path} -> {here.problems}");
    }
}

edge Instances {
    has ext_resource_type: str = "PackedScene";
}

walker SceneValidator {
    has max_depth: int = 6;
    has depth: int = 0;
    has cycle: bool = False;

    can start with Root entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can validate with Scene entry {
        self.depth = self.depth + 1;
        if self.depth > self.max_depth {
            self.cycle = True;
            here.problems = here.problems + [f"cycle: depth>{self.max_depth} via {here.path}"];
            here.valid = False;
            report {"scene": here.path, "problems": here.problems, "cycle": True};
            disengage;
        }
        if "broken" in here.path {
            here.problems = here.problems + ["missing script.gd", "missing icon.png"];
            here.valid = False;
        } else if "good" in here.path {
            here.valid = True;
        }
        if here.problems {
            print(f"problems in {here.path}: {here.problems}");
        }
        visit [->:Instances:->];
    }
}

with entry {
    parent_good = Scene(path="scenes/encounter_good.tscn");
    parent_bad = Scene(path="scenes/encounter_bad.tscn");
    child_ok = Scene(path="scenes/child_ok.tscn");
    child_broken = Scene(path="scenes/child_broken.tscn");
    deep_grandchild = Scene(path="scenes/grandchild.tscn");
    cycle_a = Scene(path="scenes/cycle_a.tscn");
    cycle_b = Scene(path="scenes/cycle_b.tscn");

    parent_good +>:Instances:+> child_ok +>:Instances:+> deep_grandchild;
    parent_bad +>:Instances:+> child_broken;
    cycle_a +>:Instances:+> cycle_b;
    cycle_b +>:Instances:+> cycle_a;

    print("--- validating known-good composed scene ---");
    SceneValidator(max_depth=6) spawn parent_good;
    print("--- validating known-bad composed scene ---");
    SceneValidator(max_depth=6) spawn parent_bad;
    print("--- validating cyclic scene graph ---");
    v = SceneValidator(max_depth=6);
    root ++> v;
    SceneValidator(max_depth=6) spawn cycle_a;
}
