## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Repeated recovery is idempotent and creates at most one valid replacement for abandoned work.
- [ ] Parent cancellation settles all descendants without deleting history or accepting stale outputs.
- [ ] Child success, failure, timeout, and cancellation have deterministic parent-facing outcomes.
- [ ] A child cannot publish partial completion effects to its parent.
- [ ] Restart and cancellation acceptance scenarios retain trace, lineage, resource, and policy evidence.
