A maintainer on the project NousResearch/hermes-agent (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #96629: [Bug]: Kanban ready/todo/blocked cards with an orphaned claim_lock are never dispatched

A card in a non-running state (`ready`/`todo`/`blocked`) that still carries a `claim_lock`/`claim_expires` from an earlier run is never picked up by the dispatcher and is invisible to every automatic recovery pass — it strands until manual intervention.

Prior reports/fixes of this same gap:
- #22926 (closed): same symptom class, closed by the automated sweeper as `implemented_on_main` — but the cited implementations (`release_stale_claims`, vanished-PID detection) cover `status='running'` only (see Actual Behavior). The sweeper also argued non-running claim states can't arise from normal transitions; the verified producers below show they can.
