```jac
"""Burst-side stale summary fields: model the L3 BC / L4 VP / Story drift scenario.

A factory tracks three kinds of primary content (L3 BCs, L4 VPs, Stories)
attached to two summary surfaces (STATE.md frontmatter, STORY-INDEX totals).
Hand-rolled machinery in the bug report incremented the primary content but
forgot to recompute the derived totals, so the summaries drifted. Here the
totals are computed by a walker that follows typed edges from each summary
to its primary content nodes, so they cannot go stale on add.
"""

node BC {
    has bid: str = "";
    has points: int = 0;
}

node VP {
    has vid: str = "";
    has points: int = 0;
}

node Story {
    has sid: str = "";
