Issue #313: Extract or copy a cell subtree between libraries

## Summary

Add a hierarchy-preserving API that copies selected root cells and all reachable descendants into a new or existing library.

## Scope

- Preserve shared descendants exactly once.
- Apply existing cell-conflict strategies and return a deterministic rename map.
- Optionally filter geometry by layer while keeping the resulting references valid.

## Acceptance criteria

- Multiple roots sharing a child produce one copied child.
- All renamed references point at the renamed target.
- The operation is atomic and rejects cycles or unresolved targets.

## Context

Current merge works at whole-library granularity. KLayout provides subtree copy/write operations in its [`Cell` API](https://www.klayout.org/downloads/master/doc-qt5/code/class_Cell.html).

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

