Models the scenario from beads issue #5887: a dependency cycle (parent-child
plus blocks) makes a naive tree walker recurse forever. We declare a small
graph of issue nodes with typed edges, then a walker traverses with an
explicit visited set so the cycle renders as a leaf rather than blowing the
call stack.
